---
/**
 * NOTE FOR THE OWNER — this comment is not rendered.
 *
 * This policy is written to be factually accurate about what the site actually
 * does, and structured the way an Australian Privacy Principles reviewer
 * expects. It is not legal advice and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Have
 * it checked before you rely on it, particularly if you tender for government
 * or enterprise work where a privacy questionnaire is part of procurement.
 *
 * Keep it true. If any of the following change, the text has to change too:
 *   - the hosting provider (currently Cloudflare Pages)
 *   - whether Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled
 *   - the scheduling provider (currently Cal.com)
 *   - the email path: Cloudflare Email Routing forwards to a Microsoft mailbox.
 *     If you move to Zoho, Google Workspace or Microsoft 365, rename both the
 *     disclosure and the overseas-recipients sentence.
 *   - the retention period, which is stated as seven years
 *
 * Bump PRIVACY_UPDATED in src/config.ts whenever this text changes.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMPANY, CONTACT, PRIVACY_UPDATED, isSet } from '../config';

const updated = new Date(PRIVACY_UPDATED).toLocaleDateString('en-AU', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Shab"
  description="How Shab collects, uses, stores and discloses personal information, under the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth)."
>
  <article class="section container">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="prose__lead">
        This policy explains how we handle personal information, and how to reach us about it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {COMPANY.name}, <span class:list={[!isSet(COMPANY.abn) && 'placeholder']}>ABN {COMPANY.abn}</span>,
        of <span class:list={[!isSet(COMPANY.address) && 'placeholder']}>{COMPANY.address}</span>.
        We handle personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the
        Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you visit this site.</strong> The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare
        receives your IP address and basic request information — the page requested, the time, your
        browser and device type — and holds it briefly to deliver the page and to protect the site
        from attack and abuse. We do not use that information to identify you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand which pages are
        read. It sets no cookies, does not track you across other websites, and reports only
        aggregate figures. No individual visitor is identified to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you email us.</strong> Mail sent to our address is forwarded by Cloudflare
        Email Routing into a mailbox hosted by Microsoft. We keep your message and contact details
        so we can reply, and so we can carry out work for you if we go on to do so.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you book a call.</strong> The booking button opens a scheduling page provided
        by Cal.com. Anything you enter there — typically your name, email address and a note about
        what you want to discuss — is collected by Cal.com and passed to us. Cal.com handles it
        under its own privacy policy as well as this one.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies. Fonts are served from this domain rather than from a third-party
        font service, so reading a page does not report your visit to anyone beyond our host.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage, security and how long we keep things</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss, and unauthorised
        access or disclosure. In practice that means access is limited to people who need it,
        accounts are protected by multi-factor authentication, and information is held in reputable
        hosted services rather than on unmanaged devices.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep business correspondence and engagement records for seven years, which reflects
        Australian record-keeping obligations, and destroy or de-identify personal information when
        we no longer need it and are not required to keep it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we disclose it to, including overseas</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not disclose it for anyone else's marketing.
        We disclose it only to the service providers we use to operate the business — Cloudflare
        for hosting, Cal.com for scheduling, and, for email, Cloudflare Email Routing, which
        forwards messages sent to us into a mailbox hosted by Microsoft — and where the law
        requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some of those providers are located outside Australia. Cloudflare, Cal.com and Microsoft
        are based in the United States and operate infrastructure in several countries, so
        information handled through this site, its booking page, or an email you send us is
        likely to be stored or processed overseas.
      </p>

      <h2>Access and correction</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask what personal information we hold about you, ask for a copy, and ask us to
        correct it if it is wrong or out of date. Write to <span
          class:list={[!isSet(CONTACT.email) && 'placeholder']}>{CONTACT.email}</span> and we
        will respond within a reasonable period. We will tell you if we cannot give you access, and
        why.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you think we have mishandled your personal information, write to <span
          class:list={[!isSet(CONTACT.email) && 'placeholder']}>{CONTACT.email}</span> and we
        will look into it and respond. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can refer the
        matter to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at oaic.gov.au.
      </p>

      <h2>Data breaches</h2>
      <p>
        If a data breach occurs that is likely to result in serious harm, we will notify affected
        individuals and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner, as required by the
        Notifiable Data Breaches scheme.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We update this policy when what we do changes. The current version is shown below; if we
        make a significant change we will say so on this page.
      </p>

      <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-h2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    font-size: var(--step-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .prose__lead {
    font-size: var(--step-lead);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .prose__updated {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: var(--step-fine);
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
</style>
